EXPERIMENT 3 – DEFECT REPORT FOR WEB-BASED FORM SUBMISSION APPLICATION

AIM
To create defect reports for a web-based form submission application by identifying and documenting software defects.

ALGORITHM
1. Open the registration or contact form.
2. Enter valid, invalid, blank and boundary values.
3. Compare the expected and actual results.
4. Repeat failed test steps to confirm defects.
5. Record defect ID, severity, priority and reproduction steps.
6. Attach screenshots and prepare the final defect reports.

CODE
This is a manual testing experiment. No programming code is required.

INPUT
Field	Test Input
Email	abc.com
Name	Three spaces
Mobile number	abcdefghij

OUTPUT
Defect ID	Defect Identified	Severity
WF-001	Invalid email accepted	Major
WF-002	Blank name accepted	Minor
WF-003	Letters accepted in mobile number	Major

RESULT
Thus, defect reports were created successfully with defect IDs, reproduction steps, expected results, actual results and severity details.
